# CI workflow

- Keep every existing step. Fix the cause of a failure, never weaken or skip the check.
- Do not add `continue-on-error`, `|| true` or removed steps to make a run green.
- Rehearse changes in a throwaway container from a clean copy (no `vendor`, `node_modules` or
  `.env`) before pushing. Record which steps were rehearsed and which could not be verified.
- Confirm which database the tests really used, not just that they passed.

## Rehearsal

```
git archive HEAD | tar -x -C /tmp/ci-clean
docker run --rm -v /tmp/ci-clean:/src -w /src/apps/api php:8.3-cli <ci step>
```

## Good

```yaml
- name: Migrate
  run: php artisan migrate --force
  env:
    DB_DATABASE: request_desk   # the database the MariaDB service creates
```

## Bad

```yaml
- name: Migrate
  run: php artisan migrate --force || true   # hides the failure
```
